  "description": "Tilecast release version names, their update version codes, and MSIX package versions. The server, Edge, Windows, Android build, and release scripts all derive a version code from a version name; every implementation runs this corpus.",
  "rule": "A name below the unified cutover (core code under 26000) keeps its legacy code, MAJOR*1000000 + MINOR*1000 + PATCH, and the prerelease suffix is ignored. From the cutover on, a name is X.Y.Z (Stable) or X.Y.Z-beta.N with N in 1..98 (Beta), and its code is (MAJOR*1000000 + MINOR*1000 + PATCH) * 100 + slot, where slot is N for a Beta and 99 for Stable. The code never exceeds 2100000000, the Android versionCode ceiling.",
